  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Acting Now for Food Security and Resilient Food Systems - Nigeria</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project in Nigeria supports food producers of vegetables, maize, potato and aquaculture from the Kano, Kaduna, Plateau, and Ogun districts in Nigeria to implement better agronomic, climate smart practices and contribute to their food security. We train farmers on Good Agricultural Practices, Climate Smart Agriculture, Nutrition Sensitive Agriculture, nursery development, Sustainable Land Use and conservation agriculture. Women and youth are supported to establish homestead gardens and become managers of newly established seed and seedling nurseries. Farmers and entrepreneurial young adults are supported to produce and start selling biofertilizer and offering other farm services, including farm inputs.</narrative>
  </description>
